    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
    "body": "## Goal\nExtend the shared import validation and Git-preparation backend for Import as workspace. Reuse the contract delivered for project import; do not create a separate workspace-only API.\n\n## Scope\n- Extend POST /imports/validate to support importKind: workspace.\n- Validate the selected workspace root without mutation.\n- Return root Git status and direct child repository statuses in ImportValidationResult.\n- For every child repository, return isRepo, hasCommit, hasOrigin, isEmptyFolder, needsGitInit, requiredActions, and blockingErrors.\n- Identify the root separately from child repositories so the frontend can explain whether the root is a repository and which children are ready or need setup.\n- Extend POST /imports/prepare-git to accept approved actions for multiple repositories.\n- Run each repository's approved missing actions sequentially, and emit GitPreparationEvent values for every repository and step.\n- Keep approval explicit: no Git mutations before user approval, only missing approved actions, and never overwrite an existing origin automatically.\n\n## Error Handling\nReturn typed, user-displayable validation errors for invalid paths, unreadable folders, unsupported folder structures, repository discovery failures, Git failures, and worktree resolution failures. Build on the remediation direction in [#3686](https://github.com/Untrivial-ai/agent-orchestrator/issues/3686); avoid raw internal errors in the UI contract.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- A workspace validation result clearly distinguishes the selected root and child repositories.\n- Child repositories that need Git initialization expose needsGitInit: true and their required actions.\n- Ready children are represented without preparation actions.\n- Partial setup is represented per repository: missing commit and/or remote must not be treated as needing git init.\n- If the selected root is already a repository with an origin remote and direct child repositories are detected, the backend returns a non-blocking warning that AO will import it as a project rather than a workspace.\n- Preparation supports an explicitly approved set of affected repositories and emits per-repository, per-step progress.\n- Tests cover an empty root, root repo, ready child repos, partially initialized children, non-Git children, invalid paths, and execution failure.\n- OpenAPI and frontend API types are regenerated.\n\n## Related\n- [#4755](https://github.com/Untrivial-ai/agent-orchestrator/issues/4755) establishes the shared project-import contract.\n- [#3686](https://github.com/Untrivial-ai/agent-orchestrator/issues/3686) documents the existing workspace import remediation problem.\n",
